{"run_id":"run_be76f5587660","schema_version":"0.1","seq":15,"t_ms":15,"text":"I found what the notes say about commentary, but the actual threshold value isn't written down anywhere I searched.\n\n**Planning variance commentary notes:**\n- Commentary is written against the approved budget and reviewed each period.\n- Any material variance above the agreed threshold must have a named owner and a remediation date.\n\n**Process:** The Finance review calendar for 2026 says the review runs monthly and closes five business days after period end. Planning submits its commentary through the finance review queue.\n\n**Threshold rules:** The notes only mention an \"agreed threshold.\" They don't give an amount or percentage, or say how \"material\" is defined. The calendar says it contains no figures. Finance is probably the team to ask for the actual threshold.","turn":4,"type":"agent.message"}
